    "long_description": "State-level injury and overdose rates for Medicaid beneficiaries, from the Medicaid and CHIP Adult Core Set Quality Measures voluntarily reported by states to CMS (2014-2023). Includes opioid use disorder (OUD: percent of adults without cancer receiving high-dosage opioid prescriptions), initiation and engagement of substance use disorder treatment (IET: percent of adults with a new substance use disorder diagnosis who initiated and engaged in treatment), follow-up after ED visit for alcohol and drug abuse (FUA: percent of adults with a follow-up visit within 30 days after an ED visit for alcohol or drug abuse), and concurrent use of opioids and benzodiazepines (COB: percent of adults who received concurrent prescriptions for opioids and benzodiazepines). Reporting is voluntary; not all states report all measures each year.",
